title ALES135 — Lotus's stereo_tube: the asymmetric tube drive carried into stereo, one shared uneven rail, the even-harmonic corner of the nonlinear class
prompt Read REMEMBER and the 1024-round itinerary + six-season double-seat; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think Next lap of this recur turn (after ALES134 stereo_fold landed and sent). The ALES134 log itself named the next mechanical laps — crush, tube, decimate to stereo. Crux-first among them is the tube: it is the DRIVE family's one member that is NOT odd, so its stereo lift teaches a genuinely new law the three prior corners could not — the inter-channel ANTISYMMETRY breaks, not just the ratio. That is the harder, more decisive rung, so I took it before crush.
think Read tube.rye (ALES82): tube(clip, start, count, num, den, ceil_pos, ceil_neg) — ALES78's pre-gain, then a sign-split pin (positive half to ceil_pos, negative to −ceil_neg). TubeError = {BadGain, BadCeiling (guards BOTH ceilings), BadRange}. Structurally identical to ALES132's stereo_drive lift with one extra ceiling to validate. Mirrored ALES82's guards once up front against the shared params and shared length (both ceilings checked into [1, sample_max]), then ran mono tube per channel; reused TubeError whole, invented no new fault or primitive.
think Wrote the self-approved design read, module, witness. Proved four laws. The distinctive stereo crux this round is 3b, the ANTISYMMETRY BREAK: an out-of-phase master (right = −left, both +2000/−2000) driven unity into (+1500, −800) comes back left +1500, right −800 — so right ≠ −left, because the map is not odd and the two ceilings differ. Under any ODD sibling (hard clip / soft drive / fold) the mirror would have held; asserted r != −l to make the even-harmonic signature checkable, not merely narrated. Added 3d, the family recognition: EQUAL ceilings (1500, 1500) degenerate the stereo tube to ALES132's stereo hard drive byte for byte, proven against drive.drive per channel. Witness GREEN; tame_style_check bans clean; width-check exit 0.
obs The DRIVE family now holds four stereo readings of the excess: pin (ALES132), round (ALES133), reflect (ALES134), uneven-pin (ALES135). The tube is the first non-odd corner, so it carries a second inter-channel law the odd corners lacked — the antisymmetry break — and this is the first stereo rung to prove it. No custody gate reached: purely local software, two bounded i16 Clips, self-approved design round. The remaining DRIVE-family lift named for stereo is crush (also non-odd, a floor toward negative infinity — its lift will want a sign-law note like this one), then decimate; each inherits the shared-map validate-once pattern.
loom witness=ales_stereo_tube_witness result=GREEN laws=4 channels=2 class=nonlinear cases=antisymmetry-break+family-recognition
file lotus/stereo_tube.rye ALES135 — stereo_tube, the asymmetric tube drive lifted to stereo: one shared uneven rail on both channels, validated once (both ceilings), four laws with the per-channel asymmetric crux (the antisymmetry breaks) and the equal-ceilings-recover-the-hard-drive family recognition.
file tools/ales_stereo_tube_witness.rish the witness — builds, runs selftest, asserts the GREEN ales-stereo-tube line.
file active-designing/20260815-034120_fill-ales135-lotus-stereo-tube.md the self-approved design read for this rung.
file lotus/README.md front door synced — ALES135 roster entry on the Status line, stamp refreshed.
recommend keep-going the stereo nonlinear class holds four DRIVE readings of the excess (pin · round · reflect · uneven-pin); the next mechanical laps lift crush and decimate to stereo, each inheriting this rung's shared-map pattern with the non-odd sign-law note — no gate reached.
